21188.sol:
We have,

e^{i x}=\cos x+t \sin x

Put $x=\frac{\pi}{2} \begin{aligned}$&\Rightarrow \quad e^{i $\frac{\pi}{2}$}=\cos $\frac{\pi}{2}+$i \sin $\frac{\pi}{2}$\\
&\Rightarrow \quad e^{i $\frac{\pi}{2}$}=i \Rightarrow e^{i^{2} $\frac{\pi}{2}$}=\langle i)^{i} \Rightarrow i=e^{-$\frac{\pi}{2}$}
\end{aligned}

$\therefore$ Imaginary part of $i$ is zero.

